examples.question_text:
Find the volume of this cylinder. Give the exact answer in terms of $\pi$, then round to two decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,-0.8)--(3.2,-0.8) (0,0.8)--(3.2,0.8);
\draw[black] (0,0) ellipse (0.25 and 0.8);
\draw[black] (3.2,0.8) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,x radius=0.25,y radius=0.8];
\draw[black,dashed] (3.2,0.8) arc[start angle=90,end angle=270,x radius=0.25,y radius=0.8];
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(0,0.8);
\path (0,0.4) node[left] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.6,0.8) node[above] {$13\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the volume of this cylindrical tank. Give the exact answer in terms of $\pi$, then round to one decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (-1,0)--(-1,2) (1,0)--(1,2);
\draw[black] (0,2) ellipse (1 and 0.3);
\draw[black] (-1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=1,y radius=0.3];
\draw[black,dashed] (-1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,x radius=1,y radius=0.3];
\draw[black,<->] (-1,2)--(1,2);
\path (0,2.3) node[above] {$4\text{ m}$};
\path (1,1) node[right] {$3\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
